\pard\b\fs20 Breaking Tunnel Ends\b0\par
\fs16\par
When digging ends, any blocking pieces of tunnel that formed break away. This lets you dig straight down onto a passage, for example. Without this rule, the clonk stops digging and hangs in the air, because the opening is too small. With this rule, the blocking pieces break out and the clonk drops into the tunnel below.\par
Script.c contains the parameters, which can be overloaded in your own scenario as needed.\par
}
